# No unnecessary comments

Do not add comments that restate what the code already says.

```cpp
// ❌ BAD
// Increment the counter
count++;

// Set status to loading
setStatus("Loading");

// ✅ GOOD — only when the why is non-obvious
// Defer decode one frame so "Loading" can paint first
pendingLoad_ = true;
```

Prefer clear names and structure over commentary. Keep comments rare: non-obvious invariants, workarounds, or external protocol constraints only.
